            <ArticleTitle>Chikungunya: acute fever, rash and debilitating arthralgias in a returning traveler from Haiti.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>418-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/jtm.12159</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The following case report details a case of chikungunya fever in a returning traveler from Haiti. The report highlights the clinical presentation and natural history of the disease, and emphasizes that chikungunya has become established in the western hemisphere, with a resultant need for heightened provider awareness.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© 2014 International Society of Travel Medicine.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
